     3	## What is proven
     4	
     5	Under the supplied reference semantics, for every finite `IntSeq` `CS` for
     6	which `bracketInput(CS)` is true, loading the exact translated body of
     7	`is_nested` and calling it with `str(CS)` reaches a Boolean `RESULT` satisfying
     8	
     9	```k
    10	RESULT ==Bool nestedResult(CS)
    11	```
    12	
    13	`nestedResult(CS)` is true exactly when the four characters `[`, `[`, `]`, `]`
    14	occur in that order as a subsequence. This is equivalent to the prompt's
    15	property: `[[]]` is itself a valid nested bracket subsequence, and every valid
    16	bracket subsequence containing a nested pair has `[[]]` as a further
    17	subsequence.
    18	
    19	This is a partial-correctness result in the Kit sense. The proof covers the
    20	exact function body, module binding, argument evaluation, loop execution,
    21	return, frame restoration, and returned Boolean under the supplied semantics.
